Build REALITY at e1986a4d31ca, which bounds the post-handshake record scan of the target probe

FORK DEVIATION: not an upstream Xray commit. The pin requires github.com/xtls/reality 9234c772ba8f.
REALITY e1986a4d31ca (#36) changes only record_detect.go and tls.go and leaves REALITY's go.mod as it
was: PostHandshakeRecordDetectConn.Read stops at a record the data does not hold instead of slicing
past the end, which panicked the probe goroutine that xray starts for every REALITY listener when
the target's post-handshake record was cut short; both probe goroutines close their target
connection; the CCS probe no longer writes the err its caller returns; and the buffer that holds a
target record grows from 8192 to 17 KiB. Upstream Xray moved from 9234c772ba8f straight to
8cdf7bf9c7f0 (47cfe99), which also refuses a ClientHello without X25519MLKEM768, so this patch stops
one commit earlier. It changes only go.mod and go.sum and applies last, after
xray-zstd-brotli-cert-decompression.patch, whose go.sum lines it uses as context; its name sorts
last for the make build_xray glob.

